# Board-owned kernel command-line tokens for Radxa Dragon Q8B.
# dragon-q8b-cmdline appends these to Fedora's existing BLS options and,
# when that file already exists, to /etc/kernel/cmdline. It never replaces
# the rest of the command line and never creates /etc/kernel/cmdline.
#
# systemd kernel-install does not read cmdline.d drop-ins. Extra tokens for
# a given machine should be added with grubby --args or by appending to
# /etc/kernel/cmdline.
#
# Only clk_ignore_unused is applied by default. Hardware-tested extras:
#   pd_ignore_unused
#   arm64.nopauth
#   efi=noruntime
clk_ignore_unused
